yle=3D"font-family:Georgia, serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1;text-align:l=
eft;color:#000000;"><h2 style=3D"margin: 0; font-size: 24px; color: #121212=
;">A WIN FOR HUMILITY AND NEAT HAIR</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Perusing the records we could find of Leyt=
on Orient=E2=80=99s 4-0 shellacking of Sheffield Wednesday on a cold Januar=
y afternoon in 2011 at Brisbane Road, Football Daily could find little or n=
o indication that the young tyro who scored the O=E2=80=99s second goal mig=
ht one day be presented with the most prestigious individual gong in world =
football. On loan from Spurs, a whey-faced 17-year-old Harry Kane marked hi=
s first senior start with what the BBC described as =E2=80=9Ca neat finish=
=E2=80=9D, stealing in at the far post to convert a Dean Cox free-kick. Eve=
n after a breakthrough 2014-15 season for Spurs that yielded 31 goals and e=
arned him an England call-up, assorted experts predicted Harry would prove =
to be little more than a one-season wonder =E2=80=93 a kind of footballing =
Chumbawamba but with better manners and neater hair. Eleven seasons later t=
he immensely likable Bayern Munich striker continues to bang them in for cl=
ub and country with such monotonous regularity that few were surprised to s=
ee him <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkL=
MEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgTkXnte6zBBQDK9V1K=
4MFYOKHly0giURgk5gNv6m62oPgVaovC2spWDj2MIlZuG8fp1rmiwFuv1ZY3_PlnqGzyb199-ig=
1QzlaQZePT-B5_7Igyc291NVZVExJE3T_GvDu-gw3hc9RZSYFNZIsH0c1HcJZptLEuR-1VdXoy_=
cG0jukaiVUqzIMvzTVOZAJncDRVlhDHWJVPQCP6Rw0GW_yHJDHiRQyPRPH_eLeBLEO0T-LRDSkb=
SGeNW73DzLeIE1/4v8/_hLOBwk3TjWlJPUBUS0O_Q/h28/h001.KsQvEOTIKIr7rXjtVSBICLIY=
_cbys7SIotKxhyQYlug" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">presented with the Ballon d=
=E2=80=99Or</a>! Ballon d=E2=80=99Or!! Ballon d=E2=80=99Or!!! Ballon d=E2=
=80=99Or!!!! by the original and best Ronaldo live at the London Palladium.=
 Not since the late Bruce Forsyth has any Englishman in an over-sized crush=
ed velvet bow tie looked more at home on the famous old venue=E2=80=99s sta=
ge.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A footballer who has <a href=3D"https://ab=
link.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgs=
zcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgNa06o6laFGnmKQUHk5n2QjIlmato7Dm11gMVD57jFM3aU=
1PfaB_eVet4ELM-0PpLMCFJtLtWsD04F5hN1dWBdazN_JiGDhaQrv_BibgVe0kb6ls30yKnh5Be=
5TggEtoYqGxxPsgkohRAzpgrujTfC_Whydj5B55eoiRRtDegfy3eXU-0DIfYXrBt8YGiGJRImbk=
k1RAbwXgkCzBa_912HR-suYuK5pjynvUe0oMPrhI/4v8/_hLOBwk3TjWlJPUBUS0O_Q/h29/h00=
1.RsmKUDzmqPEGpGxPpkpdomybb8zcUwrrU3-az4TbGKA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">wo=
rked his socks off</a> to maximise every ounce of his talent, Kane=E2=80=99=
s acceptance speech was extraordinarily long and a study in humility and gr=
atitude. And while we can=E2=80=99t say for certain that Cox didn=E2=80=99t=
 get a shout-out for the assist that set the goalscoring juggernaut in moti=
on, the former Orient winger will have had every right to feel aggrieved if=
 that was the case because just about everyone else who has appeared in Kan=
e=E2=80=99s orbit since he was a Junior Gunner got a mention. When it came =
time to thanking his wife and parents, Kane=E2=80=99s voice wavered, albeit=
 in far less comical style than that time shortly after the Mexico game whe=
n he was trying to explain what happened to Jordan Henderson in the post-ma=
tch celebrations. At the end of a preposterously long awards bash high on p=
omp, ceremony and self-importance, Kane=E2=80=99s on-stage modesty was a we=
lcome antidote to much of the bombast that had preceded it. =E2=80=9CIt sou=
nds crazy, but it also sounds pretty good,=E2=80=9D he whooped of his new s=
tatus as Ballon d=E2=80=99Or winner. =E2=80=9CWhat a special night. It=E2=
=80=99s an incredible, incredible feeling. I=E2=80=99m still just trying to=
 take it all in. It really feels like a dream =E2=80=93 the emotion, just r=
elief, joy, happiness, excitement. To have that kind of release and then be=
 able to share it with everyone there in the theatre was special.=E2=80=9D<=
/p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Presided over by Thierry Henry and Kate Sc=
ott, football gong-giving=E2=80=99s answer to Mick Fleetwood and Samantha F=
ox, Monday night=E2=80=99s ceremony didn=E2=80=99t go entirely without a hi=
tch. Proceedings kicked off more than 30 minutes late, perhaps due to the f=
act the organisers hadn=E2=80=99t realised how long it would take the great=
 and the good of the game to preen their way down the seemingly endless red=
 carpet rolled out on Argyll Street. =E2=80=9CFootball unites the world=E2=
=80=9D has long been the clarion call of Fifa overlord, Gianni Infantino, a=
nd for a while during the Ballon d=E2=80=99Or buildup there was no discerni=
ble difference between those posing on the Axminster in their glad rags and=
 those shivering in their anoraks on the other side of nearby barriers. Whi=
le few would begrudge Kane an accolade that is a bit naff but clearly means=
 so much to him, like most empty vessels these naysayers tend to make a lot=
 of noise. Online superfans of Kylian Mbapp=C3=A9 and Lamine Yamal have bee=
n vocal in their disparagement of the voting process, while more than a few=
 Arsenal fans appear to have got the hump because something-or-other about =
Declan Rice and David Raya. All concerned could learn a thing or two from t=
he message Kane posted following his win: =E2=80=9CWork hard in silence,=E2=
=80=9D it read. =E2=80=9CLet success be your noise.=E2=80=9D</p>
</div></td></tr>
